'''Cíbola''' is the seventh planet from the star Aurelius, located at the very outer edge of the system's habitable zone, orbiting between the arid [[Aztlán]] and the violet gas giant [[Amatista]]. It is a small, frozen terrestrial world, often described as a cold cousin to Aztlán. While Aztlán is defined by its red dust and heat storms, Cíbola is defined by its dark iron-rich soil and permanent frost.

The planet is currently in the grip of a global ice age that has lasted for hundreds of millions of years. Despite having a thin atmosphere, the surface temperatures rarely rise above freezing, even at the equator. Cíbola represents the transition point in the Aurelius system; it is the last rocky outpost before the vast distances separating the inner system from the outer gas giants.

Cíbola is scientifically significant for its massive polar ice caps, which contain substantial reserves of water ice. Adonian exobiologists theorize that Cíbola may have supported a subsurface ocean in its distant past, potentially harboring microbial life before the planet froze over completely.

==Physical characteristics==
===Surface geology===
The surface of Cíbola appears as a mottled patchwork of dark reddish-brown rock and brilliant white ice. The regolith is rich in iron and silicate minerals, similar to the inner planets, but it has not been oxidized to the same bright red hue as [[Aztlán]] due to the lower temperatures and lack of active weathering.

A unique feature of the Cibolan landscape are the Cryo-Dunes. These are vast fields of sand mixed with ice crystals that migrate slowly across the plains, driven by the thin katabatic winds blowing off the polar caps. When sunlight hits these dunes at the right angle, they glitter with a golden hue, a phenomenon that likely inspired its mythological namesake.

The planet possesses large, distinct polar caps composed of water ice covered by a seasonal layer of dry ice (frozen carbon dioxide). During the long Cibolan winter, these caps expand significantly, reaching down to the mid-latitudes.

===Atmosphere===
Cíbola possesses a thin, transparent atmosphere composed primarily of nitrogen and carbon dioxide. Unlike the hazy skies of [[Ciguapa]] or the dusty atmosphere of [[Aztlán]], the air on Cíbola is incredibly clear. This lack of atmospheric scattering creates a stark, high-contrast environment where shadows are pitch black and the stars are visible even during the day.

The pressure is too low for liquid water to exist on the surface, but it is sufficient to support a weak greenhouse effect that keeps the equatorial regions from plunging into absolute cryogenic temperatures during the day.

==Orbit and rotation==
Cíbola orbits Aurelius at a distance of 2.10 AU, completing a revolution every 1,120 standard days. This long orbital period means seasons on Cíbola last nearly an entire Adonian year.

The planet has a rotation period of 25.1 hours, very similar to [[Adonia]] and [[Aztlán]]. This similarity in day length across the three potentially habitable worlds suggests a commonality in their formation history or late heavy bombardment phase.

==Name and etymology==
The name Cíbola is derived from the Insulonian legend of the Seven Cities of Gold, a mythical land of immense wealth sought by explorers. Early astronomers named the planet Cíbola due to the glittering, golden reflection of sunlight off its icy dunes and frost-covered plains.

In Sanese astronomical nomenclature, the planet is known as Usuraisei (薄氷星), translating to the Thin Ice Star. This name captures the planet's fragile, frozen nature and the thin veneer of frost that coats its dark surface.

